WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.267
-A growing number
of Republicans,

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.734
including Congressman
Matt Gates,

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.934
are pushing to make Donald Trump
Speaker of the House

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.901
if they retake power in 2022.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:12.067
But aside from that, they're
laser focused on the big issues

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:14.133
facing Americans
Hot Pocket prices

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.467
and cream cheese shortages.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:17.901
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:22.133
♪♪

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:24.501
Because the Republican Party
remains in the grip

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:26.467
of an authoritarian cult
led by goons,

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.300
grifters,
and gnocchi-shaped weirdos

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.200
who are intent on staging
a slow motion coup

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.567
to dismantle democracy,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.300
there is no serious conservative
movement in this country.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.901
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:41.067
♪♪

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.234
I forgot to do examples,

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:45.734
I thought that was
shorter than usual.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.834
Because the GOP's focus is
solely on upending democracy,

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.367
they have nothing
to say about policy,

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.334
which is why ever since the
start of Joe Biden's presidency,

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.501
we've been subjected
to one moronic right wing

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.467
freak out after another,
like when they told us

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.133
Democrats wanted
to come to your house

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.834
and take all your hamburgers
and Dr. Seuss books

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:04.100
and then strap you down
and forcibly inject you

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.634
with a secret microchip
that teaches you

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.400
critical race theory
and electroshocks you

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.367
any time you try
to buy a MyPillow online.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:13.734
And now, here's the new one,
thanks to Joe Biden's radical

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:16.234
left wing agenda, decent,
hard working Americans

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:20.200
can't have cream cheese anymore.
-Did you hear about this?

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.000
Some bagel shops
in New York City

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.501
are just days away
from running out of cream cheese

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.601
amid supply chain shortages.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:29.133
-A cream cheese shortage is
hitting New York City

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:33.968
bagel shops here from one bagel
seller getting schmeared

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:38.400
by this supply chain crisis.
-Important breakfast time news

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.200
there's a schmear shortage here
in New York City

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.067
as bagel shops say they're
having trouble

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:48.300
restocking cream cheese thanks
to the supply chain crisis.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.100
This is big news here
in New York that you're running

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.567
low on cream cheese.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.834
-Now, I think they only
latched on to this story

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.334
for the bagel based pun --

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:59.000
"Small business owners
are getting schmeared

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.167
by this shortage,
so locks your doors

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.667
or you might get creamed."

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:08.400
Also, I don't think
bagels and cream cheese

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.400
is the breakfast
of Fox News viewers.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.133
They can't have all
that gluten and lactose.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.734
Are you trying to kill
all our grandpas?

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.934
But the shortage is real.

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:17.567
I asked for my regular
at the deli yesterday,

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:18.801
and the guy said
the best he could do

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.167
is lox and almond butter.

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:21.734
And then the almond butter
was so sticky

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.167
the lox stuck
to the roof of my mouth

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.434
and I spent half the morning
looking like

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:25.634
I had a second tongue.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.567
Plus, I asked for it
in on everything,

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:30.534
and they gave me this
because in Joe Biden's America,

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:33.734
that's in everything now.

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.601
But seriously, though,
is this cream cheese

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:36.934
thing really big news?

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.801
I mean, I live in New York City,
so I've heard about it.

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.067
But until my cab driver
tells me about it,

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.701
I refuse to think
it's a big deal.

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:44.200
And the only headline
I'm hearing from him is,

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.868
"any one of us
would have done

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:49.968
what Chris Cuomo
did for his brother."

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:53.100
I should note I only take
New York City cabs in 1974.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.567
I'll believe the cream
cheese shortage is real

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.000
the next time
I walk through the park

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:02.567
and someone whispers
"weed, coke, Philly's best?"

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.467
Also, can I just point out,

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.934
I feel like it's
unnecessarily cruel for you

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:09.100
to keep holding up a bagel
with cream cheese

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.467
while there's a guy telling you
about his cream cheese shortage.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:16.067
Poor bagel shop owner.
You trying to torture the guy?

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:20.367
"Oh, is this what
you're looking for?

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:23.100
This delectable
little confection?

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.734
Why we have an entire fridge
full of them downstairs

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:30.968
in a Fox News dungeon.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:35.567
It's where we put the bolts
in Sean Hannity's neck."

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:36.667
But you know what?
Fine, whatever.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:39.133
This is the kind
of silly content cable

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:40.634
news channels use
to fill time.

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:42.634
They don't have
our unique ability

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:44.834
to stretch out "Closer Looks"
with totally unnecessary

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:46.834
and perhaps even
counterproductive tangents

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.834
where we speculate about
I don't know,

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.300
what it might sound like
if, say, I don't know.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.133
Owen Wilson starred in the
movie about a college dropout

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.934
who, I don't know, inherits
a bagel shop from his father.

00:03:56.934 --> 00:04:01.734
[ As Owen Wilson ] We're out of
cream cheese. Geez, man, wow.

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:03.167
[ Normal voice ] And of course,
in this scenario, his father

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:05.334
would be played by, I don't
know, like maybe Al Pacino.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.801
[ As Al Pacino ]
Alright let's go.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:13.501
It's time to spread some butter
on some [bleep] pumpernickel.

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:17.234
Yabba-labba-loo.
[ Normal voice ] Whatever.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.534
We've been over using it anyway
to get out of these tangents.

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:21.734
So from now on, I'm just going
to say "Whatever."

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.167
Whatever.
The point is,

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.067
Fox filled some time
with the dumb segment

00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:26.701
about a supposed
cream cheese shortage.

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.701
But then the official Twitter
account of the House Republicans

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:32.067
tweeted an image
from the segment with the words

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:33.367
Biden's America.
Alright.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:36.133
First of all, you're clearly
not from New York,

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.434
because if you were,

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:40.033
you know that everything
bad here gets blamed,

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.234
not on the president,
but the mayor.

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:46.133
That's the job of being mayor
to soak up all the rage

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.300
and resentment in the city
like a charcoal pill,

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.167
so we don't all kill
each other in the streets.

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:52.801
And it's a weird time
for New Yorkers right now

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:54.367
because Eric Adams
has been elected,

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:56.968
but it's still de Blasio's lame
duck job for a few more weeks.

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:58.400
So everybody's just waiting.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.901
Poor Adams doesn't realize
what's coming.

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.067
Right now people are saying,
"Give em hell, Adams."

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.167
And then the second
he's sworn in,

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:07.067
"Where's our [bleep]
cream cheese?!"

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.000
The correct way to address
the mayor in New York City

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.400
isn't "your honor," it's
freakin'.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:14.667
As in freakin' de Blasio
let the rats steal our pizza.

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:17.200
True story! De Blasio
hands the "freakin'" title

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.000
over at the inauguration.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.601
Whatever.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:24.501
So Republicans have gone
from trying to scare people

00:05:24.501 --> 00:05:26.434
into thinking Joe Biden is
stealing your hamburgers

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.267
to thinking Joe Biden
is stealing your cream cheese.

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:31.968
And yet, that is somehow not
the dumbest food based attack

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.200
launched
this week by a Republican.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.000
Because Louisiana
Senator John Kennedy,

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.033
who despite his exaggerated
corn-pone accent,

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.834
went to Oxford
and used to be a Democrat,

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:42.400
predicted this week
that thanks to inflation

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.267
and the Democrats
Build Back Better Plan,

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.133
the price of one particular
frozen food

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:47.434
is going to skyrocket.

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:50.234
-When I first heard about
the Build Back Better bill,

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:53.901
I thought to myself, "You know,
this is satire, right?"

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:56.467
And then I took a look at it,

00:05:56.467 --> 00:06:00.834
and I was amazed
beyond imagination.

00:06:00.834 --> 00:06:03.334
I mean, it's breathtaking.

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:06.734
Trillions of dollars
of new spending, new taxes,

00:06:06.734 --> 00:06:09.667
new debt,
new welfare programs.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:12.100
The only way I know how to
improve it is,

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.234
is with the shredder.

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:18.434
It's going to fuel inflation.

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:21.000
When a Hot Pocket
costs you $10,

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.601
remember,
we're building back better.

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.901
-Does Kennedy really think
his voters care

00:06:25.901 --> 00:06:27.334
about the cost of Hot Pockets

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:30.000
or is it just the perfect
brand name for his accent?

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.801
[ As Kennedy ]
Hot Pockets?

00:06:32.801 --> 00:06:34.934
[ Normal voice ] It sounds like
a nickname you get in Louisiana

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:38.133
if you set your pants on fire by
standing too close to a grill.

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:44.901
[ As Kennedy] Looks like
Hot Pockets couldn't
wait for his hot dog.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:47.000
The fact is, Kennedy just
wouldn't sound as good saying,

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:53.267
[As Kennedy] Totino's Pizza
Rolls or LaCroix.

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:55.834
[ Normal voice ]
Even though LaCroix does sound
like a small town in Louisiana.

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:58.868
[ As Kennedy ]
You have a lot of nerve showing
your face in LaCroix again.

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:01.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.467
[ Normal voice ] Also,
I just want to point out,

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:04.133
as I have before,
but I do not believe

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:05.267
this man's accent is real.

00:07:05.267 --> 00:07:06.734
That's what British actors
sound like

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:09.133
when they try Southern accents
and overdo it.

00:07:09.133 --> 00:07:10.801
[ As Hugh Grant ] Yes.
Sorry, Hugh Grant auditioning

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:12.434
for the role of, uh,
Colonel Sanders.

00:07:12.434 --> 00:07:15.567
[ Clears throat ] You'll hear my
secret recipe when you pry it

00:07:15.567 --> 00:07:18.901
from my cold, dead hands.

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:21.501
I can definitely, definitely,
definitely do better.

00:07:21.501 --> 00:07:23.601
Dreadfully sorry.

00:07:23.601 --> 00:07:25.701
[ Normal voice ] Whatever.
I don't even think Republicans

00:07:25.701 --> 00:07:27.434
really expect people
to fall for this [bleep].

00:07:27.434 --> 00:07:29.100
They just have
nothing else to talk about

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:30.267
because they're not a party

00:07:30.267 --> 00:07:31.767
that is sincerely interested
in governing.

00:07:31.767 --> 00:07:33.968
So they have nothing
to say about policy.

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:35.467
Their only goal is power,

00:07:35.467 --> 00:07:37.701
and they're laser focused on
getting ready for the next coup.

00:07:37.701 --> 00:07:39.100
After nearly pulling off
the last one.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.434
Yesterday, a group of
Republicans,

00:07:40.434 --> 00:07:43.300
including Matt Gaetz,
even went so far as to suggest

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.834
that if they win back power
in 2022,

00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:47.234
they would spend
most of their time

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:49.300
trying to prove the unhinged
conspiracy theory

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.834
that the January 6th
insurrection

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:53.467
was actually staged by the FBI.

00:07:53.467 --> 00:07:56.000
Gates added that
they would focus on that

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.400
rather than on working with
Democrats to pass legislation.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:03.234
-We are going to take power
after this next election,

00:08:03.234 --> 00:08:06.601
and when we do, it's going to be
the days of Jim Jordan

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:10.567
and Marjorie Taylor Greene
and Dr. Gosar and myself

00:08:10.567 --> 00:08:13.834
doing everything to get
the answers to these questions.

00:08:13.834 --> 00:08:17.234
-Can you expound a little bit
on what the days of Jim Jordan

00:08:17.234 --> 00:08:18.934
and Marjorie Taylor Greene
are going to look like?

00:08:18.934 --> 00:08:20.467
-Yeah, we're going
to send subpoenas.

00:08:20.467 --> 00:08:22.200
We're going to conduct
real oversight.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.234
We're going to show up
in person and get answers.

00:08:25.234 --> 00:08:27.067
The notion that Republicans
are going to take control

00:08:27.067 --> 00:08:28.501
of the House
and we're going to hold hands

00:08:28.501 --> 00:08:30.133
in the warm spring rain
with the Democrats

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:33.200
and legislate is ludicrous.
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.200
Alright. No one thinks
you're going to legislate.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.634
But what was that about holding
hands in the warm spring rain?

00:08:38.634 --> 00:08:40.000
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.567
Is that a "Four Seasons" lyric?

00:08:41.567 --> 00:08:44.434
Is he in the touring company
of "Jersey Boys"?

00:08:44.434 --> 00:08:46.968
Because that
would explain the hair.

00:08:46.968 --> 00:08:48.167
[ In falsetto ]
♪ Oh, what a night ♪

00:08:48.167 --> 00:08:51.234
♪ We held hands
in the warm spring rain ♪

00:08:51.234 --> 00:08:54.167
♪ Then she left me
'cause I was insane ♪

00:08:54.167 --> 00:08:56.467
♪ Let's all remember
what a night ♪

00:08:56.467 --> 00:08:58.400
Wow, without a warm up.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:59.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
Without a vocal warm up.

00:09:07.234 --> 00:09:09.167
Our hair is pretty close.
I'm just realizing it.

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:14.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.801
As I made the mistake of looking
at the key and I'm like

00:09:17.801 --> 00:09:19.501
Glass houses, as they say.

00:09:19.501 --> 00:09:21.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.968 --> 00:09:23.667
And that was somehow not
the craziest part

00:09:23.667 --> 00:09:25.601
of the press conference
with Gaetz also floated

00:09:25.601 --> 00:09:28.267
an insane idea that has been
gaining traction on the right

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:30.467
that if Republicans win back
the House in 2022,

00:09:30.467 --> 00:09:32.767
they might try
to make Donald Trump Speaker,

00:09:32.767 --> 00:09:34.767
which is possible
because technically

00:09:34.767 --> 00:09:36.300
the Speaker of the House
does not have to be

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.334
a member of Congress.

00:09:37.334 --> 00:09:39.067
Several Republicans,
including Trump's

00:09:39.067 --> 00:09:40.868
former Chief of Staff
Mark Meadows,

00:09:40.868 --> 00:09:42.200
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert,

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.834
and now Gaetz
have floated the possibility.

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:46.467
And Gaetz said
he had run the idea

00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:47.901
by Trump himself.

00:09:47.901 --> 00:09:50.868
-If you do retake the house,
do you want ex-President Trump

00:09:50.868 --> 00:09:54.434
to be the Speaker?
-I would.

00:09:54.434 --> 00:09:55.767
-Have you
talked to him about it?

00:09:55.767 --> 00:09:57.200
-I have.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.133
And that might seem like
a short answer,

00:09:59.133 --> 00:10:01.400
but it's probably how much
he talked when he brought

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.701
the idea up with Trump
before Trump cut him off.

00:10:03.701 --> 00:10:05.167
We want you to be
Speaker of the House.

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:06.501
[ As Trump ]
Speaker of the House?

00:10:06.501 --> 00:10:10.234
I have a speaker in my house.
And we call her Alexa.

00:10:10.234 --> 00:10:13.000
We love Alexa, don't we folks?
We love, we love Alexa.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.133
All the answers she's got all
th-- You know why we love her?

00:10:16.133 --> 00:10:18.734
When you ask her a question,
she answers, you know.

00:10:18.734 --> 00:10:22.434
That's why I call her the
reverse Melania.

00:10:22.434 --> 00:10:25.501
Not hearing much from Melania
these -- Alexa.

00:10:25.501 --> 00:10:28.434
Alexa, why isn't Melania
talking to me?

00:10:28.434 --> 00:10:30.534
-Because she hates you.
-[ Normal voice ] Now,

00:10:30.534 --> 00:10:33.667
the point is these people's
depravity truly knows no bounds.

00:10:33.667 --> 00:10:35.868
Trump let a deadly pandemic
ravage the country,

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:37.100
leading to mass suffering,

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.400
he stoked a violent coup
to overturn the election,

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.334
and he personally
came into contact

